{"seq":1,"slug":"turning-philosophy","title":"Turning Philosophy","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/socrates/core-contributions/turning-philosophy","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"from-nature-to-man","title":"从自然到人","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/socrates/core-contributions/turning-philosophy/from-nature-to-man","wordCount":2101,"readingTime":9},{"seq":2,"slug":"the-birth-of-ethics","title":"伦理学的诞生","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/socrates/core-contributions/turning-philosophy/the-birth-of-ethics","wordCount":1976,"readingTime":8}],"introHtml":"<p>本章呈现苏格拉底最根本的贡献——哲学的转向。在他之前，哲学主要探究自然；而苏格拉底将哲学的目光转向人本身——人的灵魂、德性与生活。这一&quot;苏格拉底式转向&quot;，是西方哲学史上的分水岭，它开创了伦理学，使&quot;人应当如何生活&quot;成为哲学的核心关切。本章揭示这一转向的实质与深远意义。</p>\n"}